## 📚 Terms I’m Still Learning

| Term                | What I Understand So Far                                                                  |
| ------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| **COPY INTO**       | Loads data into a target table from files or external locations.                          |
| **Delta**           | A table/storage format used for reliable data processing and management.                  |
| **Function**        | Reusable logic that can be called when needed.                                            |
| **Cron**            | A syntax commonly used to define recurring schedules.                                     |
| **Webhook**         | A mechanism for triggering or notifying another system when an event occurs.              |
| **VACUUM**          | Removes old files that are no longer needed by a Delta table, subject to retention rules. |
| **CI/CD**           | Practices for testing, reviewing, integrating, and safely delivering changes.             |
| **Job**             | A scheduled or triggered unit of pipeline execution.                                      |
| **Task**            | An individual operation within a job or workflow.                                         |
| **DAG**             | Directed Acyclic Graph; represents tasks and their dependencies.                          |
| **Retry**           | Automatically attempts a failed operation again.                                          |
| **Rerun**           | Runs an execution again, usually after a failure or issue.                                |
| **Backfill**        | Processes historical data that was missed or needs to be recomputed.                      |
| **Freshness**       | Indicates how recent the available data is.                                               |
| **Lineage**         | Tracks the origin and movement of data through different processes.                       |
| **Least Privilege** | Gives only the minimum permissions required to perform a task.                            |

