## 🚨 Incident vs. Problem vs. Workaround

One distinction I found important is that these are not necessarily the same thing:

| Concept        | Meaning                                                             |
| -------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| **Incident**   | A point-in-time event that disrupts normal operation.               |
| **Problem**    | The underlying or systemic issue that may cause repeated incidents. |
| **Workaround** | A temporary solution or detour used to restore operation.           |

Understanding the difference helps avoid treating the **symptom** as if it were the **root cause**.

